The watchdog's subscription refresh, due: selected=auto, a running router, saved
subscriptions and no sub-update.at, so this tick refreshes. The feeds are the
closed port 127.0.0.1:9 (as in pool-seeded), so the fetch fails — which keeps
the pool and never reloads, the one outcome this sandbox can reach (a reload
with the router "up" would stop the harness). What it must show, on both sides:
the audit line `watchdog: subscription refresh — error: subscription fetch
failed: http://127.0.0.1:9/…; previous servers kept` (scheme and host only — no
token), sub-update.at written, and the pool untouched. Successful refreshes and
the reload's BEGIN/END audit lines are covered by tests/test_subscriptions.py,
whose fake router can be restarted.
